id:                     E497
trigger_tool: git
phase: device-finish|prelaunch
error_signature: fatal: cannot stat '<HMDFS worktree>/.git/branches'|fatal: detected dubious ownership in repository
severity: 2
category: git-filesystem-compat
match_keywords: Git, HMDFS, /storage, /data, dubious ownership, safe.directory, cannot stat .git/branches, separate-git-dir, maintenance.auto, gc.auto
title: Keep Git metadata on a native filesystem for HMDFS worktrees
root_cause: Process-local safe.directory configuration resolves only Git's ownership guard. A Git metadata directory created directly under an HMDFS /storage worktree can still fail native metadata probes such as stat of .git/branches. Git maintenance may also fail on the same filesystem. The worktree content and Git metadata therefore need separate filesystem placements.
affected_scope: OpenHarmony device workflows that need a real Git worktree under /storage while the HMDFS mount cannot reliably host Git's metadata directory.
verification_cmd: Initialize the /storage worktree with a task-private --separate-git-dir path under native /data, commit the frozen snapshot, run git status and rev-parse, require empty stderr with maintenance.auto=false and gc.auto=0, then remove both task-private directories.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: native-separate-git-dir
rec_description: Set safe.directory for the exact worktree through process-local GIT_CONFIG_COUNT variables, initialize the worktree with git init --separate-git-dir=<task-private native /data path> <HMDFS worktree>, then disable automatic maintenance and garbage collection in that repository before staging and committing the frozen snapshot.
rec_command: GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=1 GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0=safe.directory GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0=<worktree> git init --separate-git-dir=<native-data-gitdir> <worktree>; git config maintenance.auto false; git config gc.auto 0
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: task-private-device-wrapper
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: native-complete-worktree
fallback_description: If worktree indirection is not supported by the installed Git, place both the task-private worktree and metadata on a verified native filesystem and copy only the immutable inputs from HMDFS.
fallback_command: create a new native task root and revalidate the complete input manifest before the first launch
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual-device-validation
forbid_1_pattern: git config --global.*safe.directory|safe.directory[ =]*\*
forbid_1_reason: A global or wildcard ownership exception mutates shared user state and grants broader trust than the task requires.
forbid_1_consequence: Unrelated repositories become trusted and later tasks inherit an unbound security relaxation.
forbid_2_pattern: git init .*\/storage.*&&.*ignore.*cannot stat|mkdir .*\.git\/branches
forbid_2_reason: Manually creating a missing metadata subdirectory does not repair unsupported Git metadata semantics on HMDFS.
forbid_2_consequence: Later index, ref, lock, maintenance, or object operations can fail after the workflow has already started.
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: [E101]
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
